        "flags": "i",
        "rank": 45,
        "_why": "Above system (50) on purpose. \"For x+y+z=12 and xy+yz+zx=45, find the maximum value of xyz\" carries two = signs, so the system rule would claim it and the API would name systemCheck while extremumCheck is what actually certified the answer. The optimisation rule only fires on explicit max/min wording, so a plain simultaneous-equations question is untouched."
